l.check_schema(d,baseline)\n check['\\\\''enum'\\\\''].append('\\\\''v999999'\\\\'')\n added=model.check_schema(d,baseline)\n state['\\\\''changed allowlists'\\\\'']+=1\n state['\\\\''changed rejection results'\\\\'']+=int(result\"'!=added)\n if sample is None and not added: sample=(cid,t,u.split()[1])\nprint(state)\nprint('\"'\\\\''sample whose request can grant v999999 without altering saved result'\\\\'',sample)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"{'saved answers': 1620, 'changed allowlists': 1471, 'changed rejection results': 0, 'saved retry-note calls': 4}\nsample whose request can grant v999999 without altering saved result (93, ['v5', 'v6'], 'v3')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '131,136p'; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '145,166p'; rg -n 'retry|duplicate' tests/test_theme_block.py | head -20; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md | sed -n '161,230p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '131,136p'; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '145,166p'; rg -n 'retry|duplicate' tests/test_theme_block.py | head -20; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md | sed -n '161,230p'\"","aggregated_output":"   131\tdef openai_transport(provider, request, timeout=180, max_attempts=3):   # the default preserves the production retry behavior\n   132\t    url, _ = ENDPOINTS[provider]\n   133\t    body = json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')\n   134\t    headers = {'Authorization': f'Bearer {_key(provider)}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'}\n   135\t    last = None\n   136\t    last_http = None\n   145\t## 4. Tests\n   146\t\n   147\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\n   148\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\n   149\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\n   150\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\n   151\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\n   152\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\n   153\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\n   154\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\n   155\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\n   156\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\n   157\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\n   158\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\n   159\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\"never called\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\n   160\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\n   161\t  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\n   162\t  unexercised, not passed.\n   163\t- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\n   164\t  location, write only inside temporary directories.\n   165\t- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\n   166\t  the inner function with every argument set.\n   161\t## 5. The $0 test (registered before it runs)\n   162\t\n   163\t### T1: the product path\n   164\told-2 is replayed under poc-v121 through `replay.run`, serial path.\n   165\t- **The archive.** A scratch archive seeded with old-2's non-judge calls only, so every judge request misses it and reaches the\n   166\t  transport and the real validator.\n   167\t- **The transport.**\n   168\t  - It finds each judge request's stored old-2 call by its (system, user) bytes; the 1,620 pairs are unique (Codex r38).\n   169\t  - It asserts that the outgoing request equals the stored one in every key except the format.\n   170\t  - It asserts that the format has `strict: true` and the name `judgement`, and differs from v7's only in the four citation\n   171\t    constraints and the `$defs` they use.\n   172\t  - It returns the stored answer, which goes through the real `model.call` and `model.check_schema`.\n   173\t  - Any other request (a non-judge miss, an unknown pair) stops the replay.\n   174\t- **The four refused first calls** (e88, e3955, e3998, theme ids). Each gets the saved accepted retry answer, labelled as a\n   175\t  substitution: under strict mode the provider could not have returned the refused one. All four retry answers fit their first\n   176\t  requests (Codex r38b). The four retry-note requests are not reached and are tested apart (T1b).\n   177\t- **Pass.**\n   178\t  - Exactly 1,616 judge responses through the transport, 4 of them labelled substitutions.\n   179\t  - The replay completes.\n   180\t  - The store equals old-2's on every table, listed explicitly from `sqlite_master`, with the expected differences named:\n   181\t    timestamps, archive call ids, request hashes, config checksum and version, and new empty tables.\n   182\t    - Judgements are compared on every substantive field: view, sequence, input, rung, reasons, reference, implied outcome, cites,\n   183\t      `cites_views`, pushes, theme pushes, changed, `why_changed`, publication day.\n   184\t    - Every other table is compared on all its columns but the named ones (handovers, match records, days completed and the rest).\n   185\t  - New request hashes and the config are checked apart.\n   186\t\n   187\tT1 does not touch provider acceptance (§6).\n   188\t\n   189\t### T1b: the four originals\n   190\tEach refused original goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id `check_answer`\n   191\trefused.\n   192\t\n   193\t### T2: every stored shape, offline (evidence from archived text)\n   194\t- For every stored judge request of old-1, old-2, old-3, control-1 and linked-1, the lists are taken from the saved text. These are\n   195\t  archived calls whose store state is gone.\n   196\t- The parser can widen or narrow a list (the footnote case), so T2 is evidence from the archived text. T1 covers the built path.\n   197\t- Each answer is validated through the real `check_schema` with the v12 format.\n   198\t- Pass:\n   199\t  - all 5,389 committed answers and the 2 uncommitted valid ones validate;\n   200\t  - all 17 refused answers fail on their bad id;\n   201\t  - the population is printed as in §1.\n   202\t\n   203\t### T3: the real validator's controls\n   204\tFor all four fields, through `model.check_schema`:\n   205\t- an allowed id passes;\n   206\t- an unlisted id fails.\n   207\t\n   208\tAn empty list with `maxItems: 0` passes `[]`, and fails one otherwise valid item of the right type with an array-length error,\n   209\tnot a type error.\n   210\t\n   211\tT3 fails on today's validator, which ignores `maxItems`.\n   212\t\n   213\t### T3b: one owner of membership\n   214\t- A rendered request whose evidence quote holds a blank line followed by \"[1]\", with a real evidence entry after it. The v12 lists\n   215\t  include the later id, and `check_answer` under v12 accepts a citation of it.\n   216\t- The same answer under v7's text parser is refused. This control shows the parser case is real.\n   217\t\n   218\t### T4: sizes\n   219\tThe largest format over the five archives and over the sealed D358 archive is printed: evidence count, enum values with the\n   220\treference counted once and counted twice, and characters.\n   221\t\n   222\t### Mutants\n   223\tEach is caught by a test that passes on the unmutated code:\n   224\t- push ids left open;\n   225\t- lists parsed from the text instead of taken from the rows (the multiline-quote case);\n   226\t- `check_answer` under v12 reading the text instead of the lists (T3b);\n   227\t- `maxItems` dropped for an empty list;\n   228\t- `maxItems` removed from the validator;\n   229\t- `strict` dropped from the outgoing format (T1);\n   230\t- preflight reading the fixed schema for judge rows.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
