{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'judging\\\\.check_answer\\\\(' --glob '*.py' src scripts tests; sed -n '10679,10698p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '128,144p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"tests/test_evidence_in_view.py:76:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(ANSWER, cites=['e1'], pushes=[{'evidence_id': 'e1', 'push': 'none'}]), request_text) == []\ntests/test_evidence_in_view.py:77:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(ANSWER, cites=['e3']), request_text) == ['e3 is not among the evidence shown to v1']\ntests/test_evidence_in_view.py:78:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(ANSWER, pushes=[{'evidence_id': 'e3', 'push': 'none'}]), request_text) == ['push on e3 which was not shown to v1']\ntests/test_evidence_in_view.py:79:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(ANSWER, cites=['e3'])) == ['e3 is not among the evidence shown to v1']   # computed from the ledger when the text is not given\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:39:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', ANSWER, request_text) == []\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:40:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(ANSWER, reference='  '), request_text) == [\ntests/test_theme_block.py:89:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(base, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'toward_last'}])) == []\ntests/test_theme_block.py:90:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(base, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v9', 'push': 'none'}])) == ['v9 is not a theme in force shown to v1']\ntests/test_theme_block.py:91:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(base, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'none'}, {'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'toward_last'}])) == ['v2 is named twice in theme_pushes']\ntests/test_theme_block.py:92:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v2', dict(base, rung=1, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'none'}])) == ['v2 is not a theme in force shown to v2']\ntests/test_theme_block.py:159:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(base, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'none'}]), request_text) == []\ntests/test_theme_block.py:160:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(base, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'none'}])) == ['v2 is not a theme in force shown to v1']\ntests/test_theme_block.py:164:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(base, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v9', 'push': 'none'}]), request_text) == ['v9 is not a theme in force shown to v1']\n  - a resume-once rule may be registered only for a future comparison, before its send, in both arms, and proven on stored data.\n- **Recommendation to Alex (his to open, a new version of the frozen judge):**\n  - The version: a judge version that changes the citation format only. Every id field (cites, push ids, `cites_views`, theme\n    pushes) takes a closed list built from the exact request.\n  - The test, at $0, end to end: stored accepted answers fit; observed bad ids are excluded; an empty list is the only answer for a\n    field with no allowed id.\n  - A separate design, not part of this version: the link direction (a whole reading its own part). The keys label stand-alone CPU\n    `other`, and the direction is a judgement, which D704 left open on purpose.\n- **Not done:** no paid call after the pilot, no product file changed.\n\n## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n\n- **The question:** \"试点到此收尾（结论\"说不准\"，花了 1.70 美元）。发现了两个问题：一是模型常写出不在名单上的编号，回答因此被退回，这次对照组就是因为这个停下；二是新版本让\"总收入\"把 CPU 收入又加了一遍。下一步做哪个？\"\n  Options: 开引用格式新版本 (recommended: every id field of the judge's answer takes a closed list built from the request; $0 check on\n  stored data that accepted answers still pass and the bad ids are excluded; asking again before any paid test); 先设计重复计算的修法;\n  先停在这里.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\".\n- **Scope:** a new judge version whose only change is the answer format's id fields (D711's recommendation). The link direction stays\n  a separate design. Design, then council review, then build with tests and mutants, then the $0 test; any paid test asks Alex again.\n## What runs\n\n- **Nothing is live.** The two-week run of D563 finished on 2026-11-16 at 01:23 local (`poc/data/clean-carried-run-2026-11-16/`, draw\n  complete, ledger $3.476 of $6.00); its readings are recorded (D564, [result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md));\n  the six contested last answers are being traced at $0 (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/contested-six/`).\n- **Pipeline (replay default `poc/config/poc-v118.json`, D370, D374).** Every item reads the relevant open questions from the library at the start of its day, then extraction v74i on `gpt-6-luna` proposes evidence and questions; Jev matching with the collision judge matches them; code writes the records; judging-v7 judges changes once a day; pull mode closes due questions. There is no separate seed or coverage-start report import, and reports as source items remain eligible. This default has not completed end-to-end acceptance. The [pipeline guide](poc/pipeline-plan.md) maps stages to code.\n- **Measured:** one company (NVDA) over one 14-day window (2026-07-01 to 07-14), the judgement scored at the window end on the frozen ruler (AGENTS §7.1). Three draws of `poc-v116` against three of `poc-v108` run in the same hours: 53 against 45 agreements of 57; operating margin and capex agree in 3 of 3 draws, never judged without the coverage-start reading ([acceptance](research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/acceptance-design.md)).\n- **Served data:** the service, the MCP server and the standalone page serve the sealed three-month ledger `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828` (68 theses, 34 groups; D358), built by the earlier `poc-v34` pipeline, not by the replay default. HTTP `/library`, MCP `thesis_library` and the standalone page share the dated bundle writer.\n- **Idea API:** `poc-v118-idea` (D290, D335, D374): two discovery calls and one adoption and weighting assessment; only adopted theses with positive weights appear, and nonempty plans total 100%. The [Idea contract](poc/idea-card.md) owns its fields and the limits of its scores.\n- **Interface:** the Thesis Library and Explore Ideas workspaces, with the confidence Trigger and an Action preview (no wallet connection or order execution). The [UI specification](poc/thesis-ui.md) and the [integration guide](../poc/ui/README.md) own its behaviour.\n- **Repository:** `main` holds the product, the frozen ruler and the research records; run databases, logs and model archives stay on disk (D353), located by the [data manifest](research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md). Worktrees: `/Users/lchingen/hivemind` is the main checkout, where slice branches are cut from `main`; `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28` (the extraction branch, merged on 2026-11-03) keeps in its ignored folders the stored end-to-end runs of `poc-v91` to `poc-v95` that later comparisons read (D359); `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-run-v109-2026-11-04` is the finished judging-v8 run's worktree. Older branches stay in Git without worktrees (D359); none is merged work in progress. The clean source-text comparison and its condition-hidden review are complete; council discussion of next steps is ongoing.\n\n## Open defects\n\n1. **Competitor and customer news is filed under the company's revenue questions** instead of the share, capital-spending or custom-chip question it informs (D355; filing is otherwise about 85% right). Share facts are often not written at all, an extraction recall miss. The total-revenue question holds about a quarter of all links (D354).\n2. **One bet opened twice** about one encounter in five: the collision judge splits a seed question from an identical candidate on a fine detail (D354).\n3. **A question the standard rules out** (the lidar legislation) was proposed by the extraction and opened in one draw of three (D354).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY TO BUILD.**\n\n1. **T1 must check the actual IDs in all four outgoing lists.** I added an unlisted theme ID to 1,471 old-2 request formats. Every stored answer kept the same validation result. T1 checks where the format changed, so this bug could pass the replay. Compare each outgoing list with the IDs actually shown for that request. [T1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md:163) · [Old-2 archive](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite)\n\n2. **The v12 retry path still needs a test.** T1 substitutes away all four retries, and T1b tests the refused first answers. Drive one real v12 retry with a duplicate theme push and assert that the second request carries the same citation lists. This catches a retry that accidentally sends the old open format. [T1 and T1b](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md:173) · [Retry path](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:334)\n\n3. **A missing saved judge format must fail preflight.** V3 requires a report, but preflight’s main function ignores Part A’s return value. A missing format could still end with `preflight done`. Specify and test a failing exit for that case. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md:98) · [Preflight exit logic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/preflight.py:339)"}}
